    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0504" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/4–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-25T17:00:00+03:00">April 25, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 26—12:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1343. Re Embtels 1306 and 1307, April 23.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d372-f1"/>
                    Replying to British note of March 9 on removal of Jap assets in Manchuria
                    Vyshinski <pb facs="0505" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> made additional statement not
                    included in his reply to our similar notes as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Insofar as Japanese assets belonging to the category of military
                            trophies are concerned the Soviet Govt is unable to agree with the
                            British Govt’s view that these assets should be debited against the
                            eventual share of Japanese reparations of the state in whose territory
                            such assets are located.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
